# Spec Feature Placement

## Purpose

Keep feature coverage plans and Playwright specs grouped by feature slug.

Do not dump plans at `specs/*.md` or tests at `tests/ui/*.spec.ts` / `tests/api/*.spec.ts`.

## Required Layout

### Feature coverage plans

```text
specs/<feature>/<feature>.md
specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md
```

Example:

```text
specs/contact/contact.md
specs/sort-product/sort-product.md
specs/e2e/auth/registration-to-login.md
```

The plan slug must match the test feature slug:

```text
specs/contact/contact.md
tests/ui/contact/contact.ui.spec.ts
tests/api/contact/contact.api.spec.ts
```

### Playwright specs

```text
tests/api/<feature>/<feature>.api.spec.ts
tests/ui/<feature>/<feature>.ui.spec.ts
tests/e2e/<area>/<journey>.e2e.spec.ts
```

`<feature>` and `<area>` must be kebab-case.

The same product feature uses the same slug across layers:

```text
tests/api/contact/contact.api.spec.ts
tests/ui/contact/contact.ui.spec.ts
```

Visual checkpoints stay inside the feature UI spec. Snapshot folders stay next to that spec:

```text
tests/ui/contact/contact.ui.spec.ts
tests/ui/contact/contact.ui.spec.ts-snapshots/
```

## Multiple Specs For One Feature

Keep extra specs in the same feature folder. The filename must match the folder or start with `<feature>-`:

```text
tests/ui/contact/contact.ui.spec.ts
tests/ui/contact/contact-attachment.ui.spec.ts
```

Do not create a second feature folder for the same behavior.

## Forbidden

```text
specs/contactUs.md
specs/login.md
specs/sort-product.md              # flat at specs/ root
tests/ui/contact.ui.spec.ts
tests/api/login.api.spec.ts
tests/ui/misc/contact.ui.spec.ts
tests/api/shared/login.api.spec.ts
tests/ui/catalog/sort-product.ui.spec.ts   # when sort-product is its own feature
```

Do not use dump folders: `misc`, `common`, `shared`, `all`, `other`, `temp`, `helpers`.

Do not mix unrelated features in one folder.

Do not place UI specs under `tests/api` or API specs under `tests/ui`.

Do not place full E2E journeys under `tests/ui` or `tests/api`.

## How To Choose The Folder Name

1. Use the existing feature folder if this feature already has API, UI, or E2E specs.
2. Otherwise use a kebab-case slug from the spec filename stem: `sort-product.ui.spec.ts` -> `sort-product`.
3. Keep API and UI slugs identical for the same feature.
4. Align with `specs/<feature>/<feature>.md` when practical, but do not invent a third name if specs already exist.

Catalog-like areas stay separate when they have separate feature plans: `sort-product`, `search-product`, `filter-by-category`, `price-range`, `compare-product`.

## Agent Rule

Before creating a plan or spec:

1. check the project map;
2. check existing `specs/<feature>/` and `tests/<layer>/<feature>/` folders;
3. reuse the same kebab-case slug across plan, API spec, and UI spec.

Create the feature folder if it does not exist.

Do not add a flat plan at `specs/<name>.md`.

Do not add a new spec at the `tests/ui/` or `tests/api/` root.

When the product changes, update the plan first — see `.cursor/rules/feature-change-lifecycle.rules.mdc`.

